WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.139 --> 00:00:02.357
(slow jazz music)

00:00:02.357 --> 00:00:04.576
- You get your hair done,
you can't be touched.

00:00:04.576 --> 00:00:07.715
You're just, you're on
point for at least 48 hours.

00:00:07.715 --> 00:00:09.611
The queer community needs a safe space

00:00:09.611 --> 00:00:10.720
to get haircuts

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.939
and that's part of the
reason why I'm here.

00:00:12.939 --> 00:00:14.475
My name is Dez Marshall,

00:00:14.475 --> 00:00:15.627
I'm a barber.

00:00:15.627 --> 00:00:18.044
I work in Brooklyn, New York.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.197
The barber shop I work at
is called The Gamesman.

00:00:22.197 --> 00:00:23.520
It's kind of an institution here

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.459
in downtown Brooklyn.

00:00:24.459 --> 00:00:25.696
The owner, Frank, has been here

00:00:25.696 --> 00:00:27.915
for over 50 years.
- (unintelligible)

00:00:27.915 --> 00:00:28.853
- The clientele has been a lotta

00:00:28.853 --> 00:00:30.903
men who work in the neighborhood.

00:00:30.903 --> 00:00:33.037
It's a lot of lawyers, a lot of judges,

00:00:33.037 --> 00:00:34.701
other types of businessmen.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.706
I kinda throw a wrench into all of that.

00:00:36.706 --> 00:00:37.898
(laughs)

00:00:37.898 --> 00:00:39.690
(upbeat jazz music)

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.397
I mix it up a little bit.

00:00:41.397 --> 00:00:44.213
My clientele is mostly queer, trans,

00:00:44.213 --> 00:00:46.304
gender nonconforming, folks of color,

00:00:46.304 --> 00:00:47.200
non-folks of color.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.033
For the most part,

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.480
my clientele is the LGBTQ community.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.703
- I think, with
barbershops, it's difficult,

00:00:52.703 --> 00:00:54.239
as a woman, to walk in.

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:56.671
It can sometimes just
feel like a boys club.

00:00:56.671 --> 00:00:57.695
- It's nice to feel like

00:00:57.695 --> 00:00:58.878
you can let your hair down, (laughs)

00:00:58.878 --> 00:01:00.061
or just cut it off.

00:01:00.061 --> 00:01:02.613
- I think I'm building a
bridge in different ways.

00:01:02.613 --> 00:01:04.021
Can you be here at five?

00:01:04.021 --> 00:01:05.130
3:30? I got you.

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.026
For queer folks,

00:01:06.026 --> 00:01:06.859
for trans folks,

00:01:06.859 --> 00:01:08.202
for gender nonconforming folks,

00:01:08.202 --> 00:01:09.909
hair is very important.

00:01:09.909 --> 00:01:11.189
You keep it really crisp, or
- Yeah, crisp.

00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:12.022
- more rounded?

00:01:12.022 --> 00:01:12.855
Got you.

00:01:12.855 --> 00:01:13.688
Well you need a barber

00:01:13.688 --> 00:01:16.126
that you feel comfortable to talk to about

00:01:16.126 --> 00:01:17.534
how you want to look,

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:18.899
what's that vision that you have,

00:01:18.899 --> 00:01:20.393
someone who can execute it,

00:01:20.393 --> 00:01:21.758
but also do it in a way that

00:01:21.758 --> 00:01:22.825
they're not gonna be judging you

00:01:22.825 --> 00:01:24.574
throughout the whole process.

00:01:24.574 --> 00:01:26.281
See how it's kinda growing out like that?

00:01:26.281 --> 00:01:27.408
- I want to keep it ...
- Up?

00:01:27.408 --> 00:01:29.075
- Yeah.
- Got it.

00:01:30.212 --> 00:01:32.857
- I get to spend my day
with other queer folks

00:01:32.857 --> 00:01:35.630
in a space that, you know, 20 years ago

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:38.702
we probably couldn't
have even walked into.

00:01:38.702 --> 00:01:39.939
You know, I'm part of that story now.

00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:41.347
My clients are a part of that story now.

00:01:41.347 --> 00:01:43.699
We're part of the history of this place.

00:01:43.699 --> 00:01:45.002
We're a part of its legacy,

00:01:45.002 --> 00:01:45.835
and that's

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:48.624
that's really cool.

00:01:48.624 --> 00:01:51.457
(slow jazz music)

